   "raw_text": "Research summary documenting the historical connection between Prof. Sig Kufferath (Danzan Ryu Jujitsu) and Robert Nadeau (Aikido) in Northern California. Key findings: (1) Nadeau and Kufferath shared dojo space at 194-198 Castro St, Mountain View (the Jurian Building) starting ~1966. (2) Richard Bunch was the operational link between the two communities. (3) Bunch trained under Kufferath as a teenager, became Chief Instructor at Nikko Ju Jitsu School in San Jose. (4) Nadeau later shared space with Bunch as schools expanded. (5) This alliance led to the formation of the California Aikido Association (CAA).",
